\n\\[\nW = F\\,d = 5905\\;\\text{N}\\times 10\\;\\text{m}\n    = \\boxed{5.905\\times10^{4}\\ \\text{J}} \\;(= 59.05\\ \\text{kJ})\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**4. Mechanical power required**  \n\n\\[\nP = \\frac{W}{t}= \\frac{59050\\;\\text{J}}{3.16\\;\\text{s}}\n    = \\boxed{1.87\\times10^{4}\\ \\text{W}} \\;(≈\u202f18.7\u202fkW)\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**5. Tensile stress in the shaft**  \n\nCross‑sectional area of the solid circular shaft  \n\n\\[\nA = \\pi r^{2}= \\pi (0.05\\;\\text{m})^{2}\n    = \\pi (0.0025)\\;\\text{m}^{2}\n    = 7.854\\times10^{-3}\\ \\text{m}^{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\sigma = \\frac{F}{A}= \\frac{5905\\;\\text{N}}{7.854\\times10^{-3}\\ \\text{m}^{2}}\n        = 7.52\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{Pa}\n        = \\boxed{0.752\\ \\text{MPa}}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**6. Axial strain in the shaft**  \n\nUsing Hooke’s law for axial loading \\(\\displaystyle \\epsilon = \\frac{\\sigma}{E}\\)  \n\n\\[\nE = 200\\ \\text{GPa}=2.00\\times10^{11}\\ \\text{Pa}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\epsilon = \\frac{7.52\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{Pa}}{2.00\\times10^{11}\\ \\text{Pa}}\n          = 3.76\\times10^{-6}\n          = \\boxed{3.8\\ \\mu\\varepsilon\\ \\text{(micro‑strain)}}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Summary of results  \n\n| Quantity | Symbol | Value | Units |\n|----------|--------|-------|-------|\n| Lifting force | \\(F\\) | \\(5.905\\times10^{3}\\) | N |\n| Torque on shaft | \\(\\tau\\) | \\(2.95\\times10^{2}\\) | N·m |\n| Work done | \\(W\\) | \\(5.905\\times10^{4}\\) | J |\n| Power required | \\(P\\) | \\(1.87\\times10^{4}\\) | W |\n| Tensile stress | \\(\\sigma\\) | \\(0.752\\) | MPa |\n| Axial strain | \\(\\epsilon\\) | \\(3.8\\) | µε (dimensionless) |\n\nThese values describe the mechanical demands on the winch‑shaft system for the specified lift.'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'response_format': {'type': 'json_object'}, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7}}
